        {
            "id": "c1f51fd9-8103-418e-8e66-0d74be644c86",
            "build_id": "48aa5f56-0552-473c-8b18-1933d195a960",
            "round_number": 5,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-27T23:34:41.876274+00:00",
            "notes": "Picking up [WallVibing](item_2610ca9b-5b95-48f9-94ee-9b2bf2795ddc) is a must on this character, as it gives you free sustain as long as you're wall riding (which should be all the time). This source of overhealth stacks on top of [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643)'s 100 overhealth pool, giving a monstrous maximum overhealth with quick ways to replenish your hp if your overhealth disappears. Neither of these sources of overhealth expire over time, so its easy to spam down a corridor and wall ride to quickly build up a massive amount of shielding before diving into the fight.\n\nIn terms of items, Round 5 is where you can change the build in order to best target the enemy team. Most of the ability power purple items are good to pick up as long as you have a good enough reason to take it.\n\n[Three-tap Tommygun](item_39c5d2a4-1db0-444f-86d9-2a1e9a331429) and [Mark of the Kitsune](item_09a53e39-25aa-4f66-ba51-bedbc543a1eb) as previously mentioned are great together as a dps package.\n[Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98) is great against other speed based comps, specifically hurting WP rein the most.\n[Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) should be pretty well known to veteran stadium players as a strong way to apply a healing reduction that can't be cleansed.\n[Champion's Kit](item_8682f8c7-8811-439b-8d50-fa81cd43ddce) has a big number and is worth the cash if you can afford it.\n[Catalytic Crystal](item_3e3f4f77-cdf8-4dda-a5b0-2fb9390aefc4) is a nice pickup if you're struggling to farm beat fast enough to counter key ultimates like Dragonblade, Attack Visor, or Rampage.\n[Iridescent Iris](item_b7fb28ef-ce82-416b-8693-01c274f8df4e) has good stats attached to it, but its unique upside is a little redundant for your beat.\n[Biotech Maximizer](item_01c6dcb3-d2e2-4c57-bd21-61d7b8f939c4) is not as good as it reads because [Crowd Pleaser] does not get the cdr from it, and amp only gets a maximum of 25% cdr from the initial cast of the ability. If you're healing a lot with amp it up, it might be useful, but I think there are better items to pick up.\n[Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b) seems strong on paper, but I'm unsure of how much uptime you'll actually get out of the upside. I haven't tested it and I think there are more consistent item options available.\nIf you're short on cash, you can always opt for blue items to fill your build. [Custom Stock](item_17d633af-8bcc-4893-b865-be0a7bc66fe2), [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6), and [Energized Bracers](item_f83a1d9e-91f8-4d2c-bd62-c673b8d9fd2e) are all good pickups. I tend to avoid taking too much cdr on Lucio because its not necessary most of the time. This build is much more focused around boop which already has a short cooldown.",
